  "description": "P3.A diagnostic probe: which closed form `f` reproduces the canonical magic-shell cross-coupling residuals Δ_coupling(Z,N) when evaluated at a natural substrate value t (q_0, q_0−1, or h(q_0))? Anchors are loaded from the canonical `magic-shell-empirical-instantiation.witness.json` (computed once); each is a Δ_cat difference where Δ_cat(𝔥) := AME(𝔥) − m_e·ρ·|τ(β_𝔥)| is the substrate-derived per-atom residual. Decompositions (⁴He → 2 ³He sub-clusters, ³He → D+p, T → D+n) follow the atomic-braid-recipe topology — combinatorial, not a modeling choice. Tests four candidates from the gap-narrowing plan: log(1/t), 1/t−1, log Φ_q^{(∞)}(t), KLR canonical-basis dim. Candidates whose multiplicative match-factor is a small rational on ≥2 anchors identify structural targets for the derivation; no fitting performed.",
